  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "🎉 v1.2.0 Release - Custom Headers Support & OAuth Integration\n\n      ✨ Major New Features:\n      • Comprehensive custom headers support for OAuth, authentication, and API integration\n      • DefaultHeaders property for static headers across all requests\n      • Per-request headers via IHttpClientAdapter method overloads\n      • Fluent header management in HttpClientOptionsBuilder (WithHeader, WithHeaders, WithoutHeader)\n      • Extensive OAuth token patterns and multi-tenant header examples\n      • Header validation and sanitization utilities\n      • Dynamic token refresh patterns for authentication APIs\n\n      🔧 API Enhancements:\n      • All HTTP methods (GET, POST, PUT, DELETE) now support custom headers\n      • Case-insensitive header handling with proper validation\n      • Helper methods in HttpClientAdapter for code deduplication\n      • Improved DI container usage patterns (removed unnecessary constructor validation)\n      • Enhanced documentation with progressive disclosure structure\n\n      🎯 Key Use Cases:\n      • OAuth APIs with dynamic token management → Custom headers per request\n      • Multi-tenant SaaS applications → Tenant-specific headers\n      • API versioning and content negotiation → Version-aware header management\n      • HMAC/signature authentication → Custom authentication headers\n      • Request tracing and correlation → Dynamic correlation headers\n\n      🚀 Quick Start:\n      // Static headers\n      .AddResilience(builder => builder.WithHeader(\"X-API-Key\", \"key\"))\n      \n      // Dynamic headers per request\n      await client.GetAsync<Data>(\"/endpoint\", headers);\n\n      📚 Full documentation: https://github.com/akrisanov/Reliable.HttpClient\n\n      ⚡ Breaking Changes: None - fully backward compatible",
